# Build output and runtime noise.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
.venv/
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
test-results/
playwright-report/
/.playwright-mcp/
.eslintcache
.pytest_cache/
*.log

# One ignored home for everything the development tools cache: ruff, mypy,
# import-linter, coverage's raw arc data and the Hypothesis constants store.
# Each of them is pointed here by pyproject.toml or by tests/property_settings.py
# rather than left to scatter a dotted directory across the repository root.
# Nothing here is an input to anything: delete it and the next gate run rebuilds it.
/.cache/

# Electron build output: a 90 MB installer does not belong in git.
release/

# Nothing here today, and the point is that the first one is never a decision
# made in a hurry. A public repository is the wrong place to notice a key.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Both operating systems, because this repository is worked on from both.
# macOS writes .DS_Store into every directory Finder has opened, and ._* on
# volumes that cannot hold its metadata natively.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor state is per-person, not per-project.
/.vscode/
/.idea/
*.swp

# An agent tool's configuration directory is machine wiring: it names paths on
# one workstation and services only this workstation runs, so it is private and
# versioned elsewhere. The rule is the category, not the list — a new tool's
# directory joins this block in the same commit that introduces the tool.
/.claude/
/.codex/
/.cursor/
/.gemini/
/.windsurf/
/.continue/
/.serena/
/.aider*
**/.impeccable/

# Instructions themselves are public; their local overlay is not. `*.local.md`
# is the convention several tools converged on independently, and
# AGENTS.override.md is the one Codex reads *instead of* AGENTS.md — it must
# never reach a clone, or that clone stops reading the real instructions.
**/*.local.md
**/AGENTS.override.md
/.agents/local/

# The one test that exercises private configuration rather than this product.
# tests/test_codex_config.py reads .codex/config.toml, which is ignored above, so
# in a clone it could only ever skip -- and its comments describe one
# workstation's wiring. It stays on disk here, where `unittest discover` still
# finds it and still holds that configuration to its contract.
/tests/test_codex_config.py

# The private repository, when it is checked out inside this working tree.
# Git does not descend into an ignored directory, so a repository living here
# is invisible to this one: no gitlink, no submodule, no accidental staging.
/.private/

# The planning trail lives in the private repository. This rule guards the
# habit of writing a plan at the address it used to have.
/docs/plans/
/docs/audits/

# web/dist is deliberately committed: the desktop app and any plain browser
# open the built UI straight from a clone, with no build step first.

# Review reports and other working artifacts a task writes for itself.
# A finding that outlives its task belongs in docs/audits/ with the
# frontmatter that says whose work it was.
/tmp/
/.state/
